gpui: application UI scale separate from the display scale

Window::scale_factor stays the device scale (display scale times UI zoom).
The logical viewport and incoming pointer coordinates are divided by the
UI zoom, and outgoing native rectangles are multiplied back, so one
physical window can show a larger or smaller interface. UI zoom 1 leaves
coordinates unchanged. App::set_ui_scale stores the zoom; each window
applies it on the next draw or platform resize.

